    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d293">

                <pb facs="0292" n="284" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/315: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief of the United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Yarnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Chief of Naval Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="78" xml:id="d293-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-26T15:42:00+08:00">August 26, 1937—3:42
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 27—1:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0026. During present emergency and without reference to Cincaf<anchor n="79"
                        xml:id="d293-f2"/> commanding officers vessels operating between ports
                    Chinese waters are authorized to carry as passengers to the limit of suitable
                    accommodations American nationals to further purpose of evacuation or for other
                    urgent reasons. Number in each case to be decided by commanding officer.
                    Priority to be decided by addressees in consultation with consular officials.
                    Dependents of naval personnel under orders take preference. Personal baggage but
                    not <pb facs="0293" n="285" xml:id="pg285"/> household effects may be taken.
                    Explanation should be made of nature of accommodations and that no liability can
                    be assumed for any loss or damage to baggage.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
